

The high-level processor
NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano Super 8GB

It will handle:

⟡ ROS 2
⟡ Nav2
⟡ SLAM
⟡ Perception
⟡ AI
⟡ Anomaly detection
⟡ Diagnosis
⟡ Logging
⟡ Visualization

I am positioning the Jetson at the high-level layer, while the STM32 remains at the real-time safety/control layer.

JetPack 6.2.1 is built on Jetson Linux 36.4.4 and uses Ubuntu 22.04 as its base OS; therefore, 
I chose ROS 2 Humble for the Jetson to maintain platform compatibility. ROS 2 Humble is officially supported on Ubuntu 22.04, 
whereas Jazzy is supported on Ubuntu 24.04 and can be used on a separate development workstation.


